{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"@interface","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)MLNVectorStyleLayer","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","text":"MLNVectorStyleLayer","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["occ"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A heatmap visualizes the spatial distribution of a large, dense set of point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data, using color to avoid cluttering the map with individual points at low"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zoom levels. The points are weighted by an attribute you specify. Use a heatmap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"style layer in conjunction with point or point collection features. These"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"features can come from vector tiles loaded by an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object, or they can be "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instances in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" object."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Consider accompanying a heatmap style layer with an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" at high zoom levels. If you are unsure whether the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point data in an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is dense enough to warrant a heatmap,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can alternatively cluster the source using the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"option and render the data using an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNHeatmapStyleLayer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can access an existing heatmap style layer using the"},{"type":"